1. What is the primary difference between public speaking and a conversaiion?A. Public speaking involves a smaller audience.B. Public speaking is more spontaneous and casual.C. Public speaking requires more formal language and structure.D. Public speaking has fluid and interactive roles for the listeners.2" Which of the following is a char:acteristic of positive nen/ousness in public speaking?A. It leads to perfection in speech delivery. -B. It causes a speaker to ar.'oid preparation.C. It increases the likelihood of making mistakes.D. It energizes the speaker and heightens awareness.3. If you are preparing a speech and \\,ant to avoiii ethnocentrism, which of the folloq,ingactions should vou take?A. Use examples and references only from your culture.B. Assume your audience shares the same cultural values as you.C. Focus on your own perspective without considering audience feedback.D. Adapt your message to consider the cultural backgrounds of your audience.4" During a speech, you notice that the audience seems confused by your use of a technical r:term. How should you apply your understanding of the frame of reference?A. Repeat the term louder for emphasis.B. Provide a clear definition and relatable context for the term.C. Change the speech topic entirely to avoid further confusion.D. Give notes and handouts to the audience after fhe preseniation.5. How can critisal thinking be applied to enhance the effectiveness of your pubiic speaking?A. By memorizing your speech word for u'ord.B. By concentrating information in a one-sided manner.C. By rejecting audience feedback to maintain your original message.D. By evaluating different perspectives and anticipating counterarguments.
