27 Sarah wants to prepare an outline for her upcoming speech for a group of kindergartenchildren. The specific purpose of her speech is '" fo itfbrm nty uudience ttbotrt trttcletulechnolog1,. "Unfortunately, Sarah doesn't realise that there is a problem r.l'ith the topic \\ih1, is her topicflawed?A. \rery broad and generalB. Too complex and advaneedC. Not suitable for an informative speechD. Difficult to support with statistical data28. Identify the speech topic that may not be ethical.A. Deforestation and Its Impact on EcosystemsB. The Benefits of Composting in a Suburban CommunityC. Unethical Business Practices: Case Studies of Fraudulent CompaniesD. The Art of Persuasion. Practical Techniques fot Manipulating People's Mind29. Which of the following are effective forms of supporting materials for a speech aboutpollution?i Random claims irom social media about causes of pollutions.ii. Expert testimony about economic activities affected by pollution.iii. Statistical data on the prevalence of pollution in developed countries.iv. List of specific strategies from environmentalist on how to curb pollution.A. i, ii and iiiB. i, ii and ivC. ii, iii and ivD. All of the above
30" What is the main benefit of including statistics in a speech?A. To provide quotes by authorities.B" To make the speech more entertaining.C" To provide description and numerical evidence.D. To enhance emotional appeal and engagement.Nilai Universiw/Academic/Set 1
