36 Which of the examples below represents an ad hominem fallacy?A. I don't think vn'e should consider Selma's suggestion for the agriculture developmentproject because she is obese and clumsl'.B. The CEO proposed a new strategy for cosi-cutting, but €!€ry,6n9 knorvs he is badrvith preparing budgets, so rve should ignore his irieasC. Benjarnin claims that we should reduce rnilitary spending, but he is not an expert innational military defense. So, I doubt his words on this matter.D. The research concludes that clirnate change is real, bui the researcher is knou'n tosupport heavy industry and f-actory activities, so \ € can't trusi the findings.37. Navin includes this information in his speech about diabetes:"According to the National lnstitute of Health, regular exercise can reduce the risk of heartdisease by 40Yo. Additionally, a study from Harvard University showed that individuals *who engage in at least 30 minutes of physical activity daily have a 25o/o lower risk ofdeveloping Type 2 diabetes. Therefore, maintaining a regular exercise routine is crucialfor long-term health."What is the method of persuasion used in the example provided?A. EthosB. LogosC. PathosD. Kronos38. What error in reasoning is exemplified in the following statement?"If u'e allow citizens to own firearms for self-defense, it will cause a soci.ety full ofviolence, chaos, and anarchl'. Children will use guns! In the end, everybody dies!" rA. False CauseB. Slippery SlopeC. Appeal To TraditionD. Hasty Generalization39. What does'Ethos'in persuasion speech focus on?A. The appeal to novelty or modernityB. Emotional engagement of the audienceC. The logical consistency of the argumentD. The credibility and trustworthiness of the speaker
